# Time lock: while the sequencer plays, the grains start on the tempo grid nearest P1's density. At 120 BPM, P1 60
# is the 1/8 grid (a grain every 250 ms, 130 ms long, so they pulse), with a little reach and spread (P2 40). At
# step 16 the sequencer stops: the onsets go free (random, 0.5 .. 1.5 x the mean); at step 24 it plays again from
# the pattern start and the grid comes back; at step 32 P1 moves to 100 (the 1/16 grid), and at step 40 to 200,
# denser than 1/64: free again although playing.
tempo 120
steps 48
tail 1
track fx1
input saw 110 0.3
preset 60 40 0 0 255 0 0 0 255 0 128 255 0 0 0 0 0 0
gain 1
transport 16 stop
transport 24 play
param p1 100 32
param p1 200 40
expect sound 2 48
expect peak_below -1
